<p>Swept at 8 a.m. Pine needles back on the steps by noon. Swept again before supper.</p>
<p>That was my fall for nine years.</p>
<p>If your porch is like mine was, you know the rest. Oak leaves on the steps. Maple “helicopters” in the corners. And that fine, gritty dust that blows in under the doormat and settles into every crack between the boards.</p>
