<p>My porch needed the little one.</p>

<h2 id="air-broom">The 2-Pound Air Broom</h2>
<p>What I needed was an air broom. Something that sweeps with air instead of bristles. Air gets under the mess. It lifts the fine stuff out of the cracks instead of pushing it back in.</p>
<p>But it had to get three things right at once. Lots of small blowers only get one or two.</p>
<div class="parts">
<p><strong>1. Two-pound lift.</strong> Light enough to pick up with one hand and keep right by the door. If it weighs 10 pounds, it stays on the shelf. Walt's did.</p>
<p><strong>2. No-start power.</strong> A battery. No pull cord, no gas to mix, no extension cord. Squeeze, and it's on.</p>
<p><strong>3. Squeeze-to-control air.</strong> A light squeeze gives a soft puff around the doormat. A hard squeeze clears the steps and the walk. An on-or-off blower sends the doormat flying into the yard.</p>
</div>
<p>Light but corded? You're tied to an outlet. Cordless but heavy? It stays on the shelf. Light and cordless but only full blast? There goes the doormat.</p>
<p>All three in one tool that lives by the door. That's the 2-Pound Air Broom.</p>
<p>The one I found is called the <strong>WOODRANGER Power Leaf Blower</strong>.</p>
