<p><strong>Day two.</strong> I did the porch, the steps and the front walk. Then I stood there with nothing left to do. I hadn't felt that in a long time.</p>
<p><strong>Day four.</strong> Wind all night. Leaves everywhere. I picked it up from beside the door and had the porch clear in a few minutes. No broom. No pull cord. No phone call to Mike.</p>
<p><strong>Saturday.</strong> Mike pulled up and headed for the garage to get Walt's blower. Then he stopped. The porch was already clean. He looked at the porch. He looked at me.</p>
